VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In the Load LoRA node, I have selected Crea 2 Identity Edit V1 with a strength of 1.0. Then in the Load Clip node, I will be using the text encoder Kwen 3 VL4BFP8'

[02:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Scaled. Now, let\'s focus on the groups that have the image loaders. The first group is called Image 1, and then we have the Image 2 group. Here\'s the thing, right now you can use up to two reference images for editing, but I'

[02:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'found that using two has a lot of issues, so it\'s better to stick with just one image input for editing. So, in the Image 1 group, I\'ve loaded an image for editing. Then we scale the image to 1 megapixel'

[03:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'using a Resize Image or Mask node. You can also use 2 megapixels if you want. After that, we use another Resize Image or Mask node to make sure the resolution of the scaled image is a multiple of'

[03:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'eight. From there, the image is sent to multiple nodes. First, the VAE Encode node converts the image into a latent. That latent is then connected to the Crea 2 Edit Source Patch node, which comes from the custom node pack we just'

[03:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'talked about. This node sits between the diffusion model node and the K Sampler. Its job is to give the model access to the original image during editing. This allows the model to use the original image as a visual reference while'

[03:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generating edit, helping keep the overall appearance consistent. If you\'re using a second reference image, it\'s latent is connected to the source latent B input, allowing the model to use both reference images during editing. For'

[04:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prompting, we use the Cre A 2 edit grounded encode node from the same custom node pack as before. This node also has two image inputs. The first image goes into the image input,'

[04:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and if we\'re using a second reference image, it goes into image B. Simply put, this node doesn\'t just take our editing instructions, it also reads the input images and sends a semantic understanding of them to the Cre A 2'

[04:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'model, so the model knows what is actually inside the image it is about to edit. One more setting worth mentioning here is grounding px. This controls the resolution of the image that\'s sent to'

[04:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the vision model for semantic understanding. Lower values make the edit follow your instructions more strongly, while higher values preserve more of the original identity. So, increase it for better facial identity preservation, or lower'

[04:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it if an edit is not good enough or isn\'t following your instructions. So, yeah, the image isn\'t just fed in as a latent, it\'s also read by the Qwen 3 VL 4B model to generate that semantic understanding. And because right now I'

